## Three Levels

* Three Levels of EDA Automation
// From: research/agentic_data_science/RL_for_auto_EDA_sota_review.md:25 '### 1. Descriptive report generators (the bulk of the list) — heuristic'
// From: research/agentic_data_science/RL_for_auto_EDA_sota_review.md:40 '### 3. Pipeline search / cleaning / feature engineering — search-based'
// From: research/agentic_data_science/agentic_data_science.report.md:76 '# 4. Research Trend: Agents as Search Systems'
// From: book_springer/lectures_source/Lesson02.1_From_Data_Science_To_Decision_Science.smd:72 '* The Analytics Maturity Ladder'

\begingroup \scriptsize
```{=typst}
#styled-table(
  headers: ("Level", "Search space", "Objective", "Output", "Examples"),
  rows: (
    ("Profilers and rules", "None: fixed checks", "None", "Report on every column", "ydata-profiling, Sweetviz, skimr"),
    ("AutoML", "Predefined: cleaning steps, features, models", "Fixed score chosen by a human", "Best pipeline", "AlphaClean, featuretools, TPOT"),
    ("LLM agents", "Open: any analysis that code can express", "Implicit, often unstated", "Notebook, charts, claims", "LIDA, Data Interpreter, DS-STAR"),
  ),
  col-widths: (1fr, 1.4fr, 1.1fr, 1fr, 1.3fr),
  bold-first-col: true,
)
```
\endgroup

- @Comparison@: each level trades control for coverage
  - _Profilers_: cheap and reproducible, but blind to anything outside the rule
    set
  - _AutoML_: searches hard, but only inside the space and objective that a
    human chose
  - _LLM agents_: choose what to look at, write the code, and interpret the
    result

- @Key idea@: data science agents are search systems over possible analyses,
  closer to AutoML than to chatbots

* Automation Widens the Search
// From: research/agentic_data_science/agentic_data_science.report.md:76 '# 4. Research Trend: Agents as Search Systems'
// From: //notes1/notes/IN_PROGRESS.finance.Advances_in_Financial_ML.de_Prado.2018.md:1536 '* The most pervasive mistake in financial research'

::: columns
:::: {.column width=60%}
- @Intuition@: each level runs more analyses on the same history
  - _Profiler_: one fixed report, the same for any dataset
  - _AutoML_: hundreds to thousands of scored configurations
  - _Agent_: an open-ended chain of plots, tests, transforms, and subsets

- @Problem@: in finance every analysis of the same history is a trial
  - About 20 rounds of _"take data, run ML, backtest, repeat"_ produce a
    false discovery at 5% confidence

- @Key idea@: automation is safe for _checking_ data and dangerous for
  _searching_ it
  - The same agent should run every check, but count every hypothesis it
    tests
::::
:::: {.column width=40%}

```graphviz
digraph Levels {
    bgcolor="transparent";
